                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough continues moving across southeast coastal parts of SA this evening into Thursday. A weak high pressure system centred over western NSW will slowly move east while maintaining a ridge over SA until the weekend. A strong cold front will begin to move into the Bight and track east over the state from Saturday into Sunday.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
